# Agent 0.0.30 release checkpoint

Agent 0.0.30 is published and registry-confirmed on 2026-10-11. Its verified source remains on agent main at `ee734c30151c7d431e480aff7a0d54306d387f13`; the push fast-forwarded main. The user subsequently authorized release independently, superseding the earlier publication hold. The published archive matches the complete verified archive. See [publication identity](publication.md). Desk published-package pins and checks remain pending the owning session's X2-compatible Ollama release.

## Record behavior and compliance

The release supplies the measured briefing and per-topic records method through `createLedger`. Integration completed the remaining phase-2 units, shared setup and barrel changes, guide proofs, and confirmed supplementary test repairs. The integrated adversarial review and its corrective controls closed before the final independent release gates. Unknown conversation-section reads remain silent; invalid section caps reject `NaN`. Fractional section caps retain at most their ceiling, and positive infinity remains accepted.

Compaction retains whole exchanges and does not fold the newest request or its following messages. A cut inside the first exchange folds nothing. The conversation rollup is removed: its options, getter, event, snapshot summary, and reference summary line are absent. A 0.0.29 snapshot is accepted without using its rollup summary. Section compaction, section summaries, view recaps, and reference excerpts remain.

The trim rulings remove unused ledger note configuration, recall-description configuration, unused agent option overrides, the unused gauge measurement member, the stock selection handler and its exclusive closure, unused scope descriptions, and the conversation rollup. The selection seam, replay, recorded judgments, tool-call correlation, thinking, and instruction-manager close remain. The gauge field is `overhead`; provider encoding uses `encode`.

## Record independent evidence

The final `prepublishOnly` chain exited 0 in 43,574 ms. It passed 1,857 tests with 2 applicability skips, including 132 guide proofs and 9 distribution tests. The skipped policy comparison applies only to a workspace authoring its writing rule; the skipped negative extractor test is inapplicable because the extractor is installed. Format, lint, type, and build gates passed in that chain.

The normalized replay passed 108 of 108 tests in 6,279 ms. The raw comparison captured 618 requests per build over the recorded copies with no differences or incomplete copies, in 5,784 ms. Agent and judge mutation controls each detected an injected request-body difference. Raw identity covers serialized request bodies through the retained encoder and judge transport; it excludes calibration and status exchanges and does not assert identity to a different provider implementation.

The release entry SHA-256 is `8f040acf72b6426246b79e5c2f31d3644291e4c08f49434ad1224e16f176311d`. The declaration SHA-256 is `f6f28cab8a2d417510e68f308563f1f53eb86b600e0a57208799adc8d783d171`. The release comparison ruled material artifact change with unchanged runtime dependency ranges. The devDependency and scaffold-owned files use published scaffold 0.0.100.

## Carry consumer work

The desk gauge migration is committed and pushed on its session branch at `29c7f6bf919a50c830ea9d07a34209fd69ddbf23`. Independent gates against packed agent and patched Ollama artifacts passed type checks, lint, format, build, and 532 tests with 4 applicability skips. The test launcher took 241,760 ms. Registry copies were restored after that proof. The published agent and Ollama re-pins, lockfile refresh, and published-artifact gates remain pending. The desk default branch was not changed.

The Ollama X2 patch is preserved in `consumers/ollama-x2.patch`, with base, patch, and build identities in `consumers/ollama-x2.json`. `git apply --check` passed against the recorded clean base. It includes encoding and replay forwarding, removal of provider framing, conversation-reference updates, related tests, and the matching agent guide. Replay filters provider input; the Ollama mapper still omits stored reasoning from its wire representation. That limitation is not repaired by the patch.

Independent patched-Ollama gates passed type, lint, format, build, and 811 tests with 2 applicability skips; the test launcher took 22,338 ms. Live-service gates were outside that unit. The patch does not change manifest versions or pins. After agent publication, its owner must re-pin agent, refresh the lock, rule the Ollama bump, verify the published artifact and live service, and publish with separate authority. No Ollama publication is claimed. Machine-generated packed-artifact hashes are in `consumers/packed-hashes.json`.

## Accept the release-records relocation

The typed archived driver lives in `harness/bench4`. Independent review found no supported defect in relocation, measured-input custody, offline refusal, or scoped contracts. Independent Windows verification passed all 8 dry copies with zero driver fetches and zero observed request dispatches. Type, lint, format, and 8 focused tests passed; the capped chain exited 0 in 5,107 ms. Source and protected-input inventories compared 1,706 files without changes.

The preserved archive lacks the raw a4 reference input. The actual reference command refuses before writing; reference-copy success and non-overwrite are proved only with owned inert rows and the actual driver. Path checks cover stable filesystem ancestors, including real Windows junctions and dangling links. They are not atomic protection against hostile concurrent directory replacement. Linux behavior was not measured.

The snapshot custody record identifies 161 original tracked paths before removal: 71 byte-identical retained twins, 6 relocated script twins, 80 historical backup variants, and the original class, entry, constants, and helpers. The historical variants and original driver remain recoverable from the recorded Git commit and blob identities; they are not represented as unchanged runtime copies. The recovered a5 raw runs and wire evidence remain tracked. Aggregate experiment files stay on the session branch.

The stored X2 unified patch retains its exact bytes. Default Git whitespace inspection flags patch context prefixes, including blank context lines and spaces before tab-indented source. Those prefixes are patch syntax and remain unchanged; the artifact's apply check and digest establish its custody. The vendored declaration also retains generated whitespace and CRLF bytes required by the recorded artifact hash.
